taskwarrior-3.3.0-x86_64-linux-gnu.tar.gz is a local build of Taskwarrior 3.3.0
from the unmodified source release:
https://github.com/GothenburgBitFactory/taskwarrior/releases/download/v3.3.0/task-3.3.0.tar.gz
The binary is stripped. SOURCE.json records its compiler, dependencies and
build commands. Its MIT licence and the libshared licence are preserved in
LICENSES/taskwarrior.txt and LICENSES/libshared.txt. Rust dependency versions,
licences and complete licence texts are in LICENSES/rust-dependencies.txt.

The shared runtime uses libfaketime 0.9.12 to provide a fixed wall clock.
Its GPL version 2 text is LICENSES/libfaketime.txt. Complete corresponding
source for this unmodified component is available at:
https://github.com/wolfcw/libfaketime/archive/refs/tags/v0.9.12.tar.gz
The Dockerfile verifies the archive checksum and builds it with make; the
library and its COPYING file are installed under /usr/local/lib/faketime.

start.sh, task, sandbox.py and solve.sh are separate launcher and packaging
files. sandbox.py restricts process execution and filesystem access with
Landlock; neither product's source is patched. This distribution is not
affiliated with or endorsed by either upstream project.

Installed executables have mode 0555. The launcher creates execute-only copies
inside the private TMPDIR before applying Landlock; the running program can
execute those copies but cannot read them or the installed implementation as
data. These temporary copies contain unchanged upstream executable bytes.
